{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>I am YHWH your Elohim who brought you out.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: 'I am He who distinguished in Egypt between the drop of a firstborn and the drop that is not of a firstborn; I am destined to exact payment from the lender who takes his money in interest and says, 'they are a Cuthean's,' and this is what is said: ״אל תקח מאתו נשך ותרבית ויראת מאלהיך״ — you shall not take from him interest or increase, and you shall fear your Elohim. And likewise He mentioned concerning the slave: ״לא תרדה בו בפרך ויראת מאלהיך״ — you shall not rule over him with rigor, and you shall fear your Elohim. And He said: לא תרדה בו בפרך — he should not say to him, 'Warm the cup for me,' when he does not need it; 'Hoe under the vine until I come' — perhaps you will say, who knows the matter, whether it is necessary or not? Behold, the matter is given over to the heart; therefore it says concerning it: ויראת מאלהיך.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:27.140630388Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}